course: dictionary
lesson: 12404
title: Curved shapes and curved words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Curved means bent in a smooth, round shape, with no straight lines and no sharp corners. «The road curved gently round the lake.» The road does not run straight. It bends in a smooth arc, like part of a circle.
explain: Curved can also be a verb, the past of curve. «The river curved to the left.» Here curved tells you what the river did: it moved in a bend. Curve, curves and curving work the same way.
explain: Look at the words around curved to check its meaning. «The bottle has a curved neck and a flat base.» Smooth, round and no sharp corners are all clues. Swap in your meaning: a round neck fits the sentence, so curved is about shape.
fact: «Curved» means bent in a smooth round shape, not straight.
fact: A circle has one curved side.
fact: A cylinder has two flat faces and one curved surface.
fact: A sphere is all curved, with no flat faces or straight edges.
fact: In science, light bends on curved mirrors and lenses.
exercise: «The shell had a smooth, curved edge.» What does curved mean here? | Rough, with lots of holes | *Bent in a smooth round shape | Straight and flat | Sharp and pointed
exercise: Which shape has one curved side? | A cube | A square | *A circle | A triangle
exercise: «The cyclist slowed down on the curved road.» Why did the cyclist slow down? | Because the road was covered in gold | *Because the road bends, so it is safer to go slowly | Because the road was straight and flat | Because the cyclist wanted a rest for a long time
test: Which word is the past of curve? | curving | curves | curve | *curved
test: «The river curved around the hill.» What does curved around suggest? | Dried up completely | Stopped at the hill | *Went round in a bend | Went straight over the top
exam: A cylinder has two flat faces and how many curved surfaces? | Four | Two | Zero | *One
